<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/knowledge/level5-tf-distributions-only> {
 ex:dist-t-view a cd:ExperimentParameter ; cd:position 20 ; cd:parameterKey "view" ; skos:prefLabel "Distribution construction and shape"@en ; cd:numericValue 4.0 ; cd:parameterMinimum 4.0 ; cd:parameterMaximum 4.0 ; cd:parameterStep 1.0 ; cd:adjustableParameter false ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-f-view a cd:ExperimentParameter ; cd:position 20 ; cd:parameterKey "view" ; skos:prefLabel "Distribution construction and ordered degrees of freedom"@en ; cd:numericValue 3.0 ; cd:parameterMinimum 3.0 ; cd:parameterMaximum 3.0 ; cd:parameterStep 1.0 ; cd:adjustableParameter false ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-t-n2 a cd:ExperimentParameter ; cd:position 1 ; cd:parameterKey "n" ; skos:prefLabel "Measurements per complete series"@en ; cd:numericValue 2.0 ; cd:parameterMinimum 2.0 ; cd:parameterMaximum 200.0 ; cd:parameterStep 1.0 ; cd:adjustableParameter true ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-t a cd:ChartDefinition ; skos:prefLabel "A random estimated denominator creates heavier tails"@en ; cd:body "- Simulate independent normal series; true SD stays 0.10 mg/L.\n- Divide each standardized mean by its own estimated SD factor.\n- Compare the resulting Student density with the normal density."@en ; cd:chartType cd:ScientificExperiment ; cd:experimentKind "student" ; cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:dist-t-n2, ex:rx-M, ex:rx-sigma, ex:rx-seed, ex:dist-t-view ; cd:xAxisLabel "Studentized mean departure"@en ; cd:yAxisLabel "Density"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-t-compare a cd:ChartDefinition ; skos:prefLabel "More degrees of freedom approach the normal density"@en ; cd:body "- Compare two Student densities with the standard normal.\n- More measurements stabilize the estimated denominator.\n- Shape comparison only; no observed sample is changed."@en ; cd:chartType cd:ScientificExperiment ; cd:experimentKind "student" ; cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:p1-n4, ex:p1-Mreference, ex:rx-sigma, ex:p1-seed-reference, ex:p1-comp30, ex:dist-t-view ; cd:xAxisLabel "Student variable"@en ; cd:yAxisLabel "Density"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-f a cd:ChartDefinition ; skos:prefLabel "Independent variance estimates form a random ratio"@en ; cd:body "- Independent normal groups; equal true variances.\n- Sample variances differ randomly, so their ratio varies.\n- Reverse the ratio to exchange the ordered degrees of freedom."@en ; cd:chartType cd:ScientificExperiment ; cd:experimentKind "f-ratio" ; cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:rx-nA, ex:rx-nB, ex:rx-M, ex:rx-sigma, ex:rx-seed, ex:rx-reverse, ex:dist-f-view ; cd:xAxisLabel "Ratio of independent sample variances"@en ; cd:yAxisLabel "Density"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-f-df a cd:ChartDefinition ; skos:prefLabel "Numerator and denominator have separate degrees of freedom"@en ; cd:body "- Ten B measurements, six A measurements: ordered df 9,5 for B/A.\n- Reverse to A/B: ordered df 5,9.\n- Compare positive, right-skewed densities, not group means."@en ; cd:chartType cd:ScientificExperiment ; cd:experimentKind "f-ratio" ; cd:hasExperimentParameter ex:rx-nA, ex:p1-nB10, ex:rx-M, ex:rx-sigma, ex:rx-seed, ex:rx-reverse, ex:dist-f-view ; cd:xAxisLabel "Ratio of independent sample variances"@en ; cd:yAxisLabel "Density"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-devices-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Two independent groups, two sample variances"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-devices-h a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:dist-devices-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-square a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "Squaring removes the sign and gives an F distribution"@en ; cd:latex "T=\\frac{Z}{\\sqrt{Q/\\nu}}\\sim t_\\nu,\\qquad T^2=\\frac{Z^2/1}{Q/\\nu}\\sim F_{1,\\nu}" ; cd:body "An independent standard-normal variable squared has a chi-square distribution with one degree of freedom. The ratio of independent chi-square quantities divided by their degrees of freedom defines the F distribution."@en ; cd:hasSymbol ex:dist-square-symbol ; dct:hasPart ex:dist-square-legend ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-square-legend a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:dist-square-entry ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-square-entry a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Independent normal and chi-square variables"@en ; dct:references ex:dist-square-symbol ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-square-symbol a cd:MathSymbol ; cd:symbol "squared Student variable" ; cd:mathNotation "T,Z,Q,\\nu,t_\\nu,F_{1,\\nu}" ; cd:body "T is a random Student variable. Z is standard normal, with mean zero and variance one; Q is an independent chi-square variable with positive degrees of freedom nu. The square root is the positive root; division by nu normalizes Q by its degrees of freedom. Superscript two denotes squaring; Z squared has chi-square distribution with one degree of freedom, so division by one makes its normalization explicit. T squared is nonnegative and has F distribution with numerator degrees of freedom one and denominator degrees of freedom nu. Lowercase t names the Student distribution, not an observed value. F names the F distribution. Subscripts label degrees of freedom, in numerator-then-denominator order for F; comma separates these parameters. All variables and degrees of freedom are dimensionless. Equality states identities; tilde means distributed as."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-square-h a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:tf-square-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-square-f a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:dist-square ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-square-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l5-f-distribution ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-f ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:dist-square-h, ex:dist-square-f ; cd:narration "Connect the distributions by squaring a Student variable. Squaring a standard normal supplies the independent chi-square numerator with one degree of freedom. No observed statistic or inference is needed."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

 ex:dist-t-intro-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "From a sample mean to a standardized random quantity"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-t-intro-flow a cd:FlowDiagram ; skos:prefLabel "Repeat the complete mean-and-SD experiment"@en ; cd:body "The population stays fixed. Each new sample produces a new mean, a new estimated standard error and one standardized value."@en ; cd:hasDiagramNode ex:dist-t-draw, ex:dist-t-estimate, ex:dist-t-standardize, ex:dist-t-collect ; cd:hasDiagramEdge ex:dist-t-edge1, ex:dist-t-edge2, ex:dist-t-edge3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-t-draw a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Take six measurements"@en ; cd:body "Independent normally distributed results from one fixed population."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-t-estimate a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "Estimate mean and SD"@en ; cd:body "Both estimates change from sample to sample."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-t-standardize a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "Standardize the mean"@en ; cd:body "Center at the true mean; divide by the estimated standard error."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-t-collect a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 4 ; skos:prefLabel "Collect, repeat, plot"@en ; cd:body "One standardized value per complete sample. What distribution appears?"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-t-edge1 a cd:DiagramEdge ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "estimate"@en ; cd:sourceNode ex:dist-t-draw ; cd:targetNode ex:dist-t-estimate ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-t-edge2 a cd:DiagramEdge ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "center and scale"@en ; cd:sourceNode ex:dist-t-estimate ; cd:targetNode ex:dist-t-standardize ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-t-edge3 a cd:DiagramEdge ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "one value"@en ; cd:sourceNode ex:dist-t-standardize ; cd:targetNode ex:dist-t-collect ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-t-intro-formula a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "A mean standardized with its estimated standard error"@en ; cd:latex "T=\\frac{\\bar X-\\mu}{S/\\sqrt n},\\qquad n=6" ; dct:hasPart ex:dist-t-intro-legend ; cd:hasSymbol ex:dist-t-intro-symbol ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-t-intro-legend a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:dist-t-intro-entry ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-t-intro-entry a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "A random numerator and a random denominator"@en ; dct:references ex:dist-t-intro-symbol ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-t-intro-symbol a cd:MathSymbol ; cd:symbol "standardized sample mean" ; cd:mathNotation "T,\\bar X,\\mu,S,n" ; cd:body "T is the random dimensionless standardized mean. Bar X is the random sample mean; the bar denotes averaging. Mu is the fixed true population mean, not a tested reference. S is the positive random sample SD estimated from the same n independent identically distributed normal measurement results, using n minus one in its variance estimate. Bar X, mu and S use mg/L. Lowercase n is the dimensionless sample count, six here; the positive square root of n scales S to the estimated standard error of the mean. Minus centers the mean; the fraction divides its departure by that estimated standard error. Equality defines T and specifies the count; comma separates these statements. Across independent complete samples, both mean and SD estimates vary while the population remains fixed."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-t-intro-h a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:dist-t-intro-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-t-intro-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:dist-t-intro-flow ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DiagramRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-t-intro-f a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:dist-t-intro-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-t-intro-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l5-student-t ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-t ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:dist-t-intro-h, ex:dist-t-intro-v, ex:dist-t-intro-f ; cd:narration "Start with an estimated mean. Ask what happens when its centered departure is divided by its estimated standard error, not the known SD of one measurement result. Repeat the entire six-measurement experiment, calculating both mean and SD anew each time. The next slide displays the distribution of the collected standardized values. The true mean supplies the centering in this sampling experiment; this is not a hypothesis test."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

 ex:dist-f-intro-title a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "From two sample variances to a random ratio"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-f-intro-flow a cd:FlowDiagram ; skos:prefLabel "Repeat two independent variance-estimation experiments"@en ; cd:body "Each independent pair of samples produces two variance estimates and one normalized ratio. Repeat the complete pair, not just one denominator."@en ; cd:hasDiagramNode ex:dist-f-draw, ex:dist-f-estimate, ex:dist-f-normalize, ex:dist-f-collect ; cd:hasDiagramEdge ex:dist-f-edge1, ex:dist-f-edge2, ex:dist-f-edge3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-f-draw a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Draw two independent samples"@en ; cd:body "Six normally distributed measurement results per group. Population means may differ."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-f-estimate a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "Estimate both variances"@en ; cd:body "Use each sample's own estimated mean."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-f-normalize a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "Normalize and divide"@en ; cd:body "Normalize each estimate by its true variance; take B over A."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-f-collect a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 4 ; skos:prefLabel "Collect, repeat, plot"@en ; cd:body "One ratio per independent sample pair. Equal true variances cancel."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-f-edge1 a cd:DiagramEdge ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "estimate"@en ; cd:sourceNode ex:dist-f-draw ; cd:targetNode ex:dist-f-estimate ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-f-edge2 a cd:DiagramEdge ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "normalize"@en ; cd:sourceNode ex:dist-f-estimate ; cd:targetNode ex:dist-f-normalize ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-f-edge3 a cd:DiagramEdge ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "one ratio"@en ; cd:sourceNode ex:dist-f-normalize ; cd:targetNode ex:dist-f-collect ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-f-intro-formula a cd:MathExpression ; cd:formulaLabel "The ordered ratio of two normalized variance estimates"@en ; cd:latex "F=\\frac{S_B^2/\\sigma_B^2}{S_A^2/\\sigma_A^2}" ; dct:hasPart ex:dist-f-intro-legend ; cd:hasSymbol ex:dist-f-intro-symbol ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-f-intro-legend a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:dist-f-intro-entry ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-f-intro-entry a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Two independent estimates; numerator B, denominator A"@en ; dct:references ex:dist-f-intro-symbol ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-f-intro-symbol a cd:MathSymbol ; cd:symbol "normalized variance ratio" ; cd:mathNotation "F,S_B^2,\\sigma_B^2,S_A^2,\\sigma_A^2" ; cd:body "F is the random dimensionless ratio. Subscripts A and B identify two independent groups, with B in the numerator and A in the denominator. S squared denotes a random sample variance calculated about that sample's estimated mean, with sample count minus one in the denominator. Sigma squared denotes the corresponding fixed positive true population variance. Squaring converts an SD to a variance; all variances use (mg/L) squared. Each inner division normalizes a sample variance by its true variance, yielding a dimensionless quantity; the outer fraction divides the normalized B estimate by the independent A estimate. Equality defines F. Measurement results within each group are independent and identically distributed normal variables; the groups are independent of one another. Means need not be equal. With six measurements per group both degrees of freedom are five. If the true variances are equal, their scale factors cancel and the normalized ratio equals the B-over-A sample-variance ratio used in the following simulation."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-f-intro-h a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:dist-f-intro-title ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-f-intro-v a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:dist-f-intro-flow ; cd:communicativeRole cd:DiagramRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-f-intro-f a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:dist-f-intro-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:dist-f-intro-scene a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l5-f-distribution ; dct:subject ex:l5-topic-f ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:dist-f-intro-h, ex:dist-f-intro-v, ex:dist-f-intro-f ; cd:narration "Introduce the repeated experiment before examining two example groups. Each independent pair of normal samples supplies two sample variances. Divide each by its own true variance before taking the ordered B-over-A ratio. Under equal true variances this reduces to the sample-variance ratio in the following experiment. Repeated pairs reveal a distribution, not a decision about the two example groups."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
}
